## Lore

The Swamp-Sludger is a primitive reptilian humanoid of the wilderness with
roughly the understanding of a young child. Sludgers are shy and keep away
from people, except to steal food and anything bright and shiny; they fight
only when provoked, threatened or attacked. For all their frightening looks
they are gentle, and have been known to carry lost children and pets to
safety. They are also a nuisance, raiding camps for food, trinkets and
machine parts they cannot use, and they love magic items.

They live by gathering, fishing and theft, travel alone or in small groups,
and rarely gather in clans of more than about thirty. A few fall in with
pirates or bandits, but most avoid other races. As player characters they
start out shy, naive and curious, with a firm sense of right and wrong and
no idea of laws or manners.

## GM Notes

Also known as Sludger and Old Man of the Swamp. Size 5-6 feet (1.5 to 1.8
m); weight 140-200 pounds (63 to 90 kg). Life span 4D6+72 years; mature at
12; lay 1D6 eggs. Most wear little clothing or armor; the partial armor they
start with has 4D6+28 M.D.C. Slave market value 2D6x1,000 credits as labor,
warriors and gladiators.

Enemies: Coalition and Free Quebec soldiers, who kill them on sight, and
other dangerous humanoids and predators. Allies: none as such, though they
befriend anyone who is kind to them or fights a common enemy.

Habitat: marshlands, bayous and everglades of the South, and parts of
Michigan and Ontario.
